# OSS Match — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and populate the values for local development.
# Never commit .env.local to version control.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Application GitHub Credential (Server-Side Only)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GITHUB_API_TOKEN is an application credential used to authenticate requests
# to the GitHub REST API (increasing the rate limit from 60 req/hr to 5,000 req/hr).
#
# NOTE: We use GITHUB_API_TOKEN rather than GITHUB_TOKEN to prevent collision
# with GitHub Actions' automatic, internal GITHUB_TOKEN.
#
# Create a personal access token at: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# Scopes needed: none (OSS Match accesses only public data in V1).
#
# SECURITY REQUIREMENTS:
# - Server-side only: never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# - Never commit this token to git.
# - Never log or print this token.
# - Never expose this token to client JavaScript bundles.
# - Never include this token in fixtures, mock files, or snapshots.
GITHUB_API_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Application URL (Used for absolute metadata and canonical links)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
